.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt FSD-UFS 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsd-ufs
.Nd RavenBSD read-only UFS filesystem server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
registers the
.Dq ufs:
scheme, opens one GPT partition from a
.Dq block:
device, mounts it read-only through the
.Dq ufs-core
library, and serves the tree with the
.Dq file:
protocol that
.Xr vfsd 8
mounts.
The initial mount is read-only; K55 adds the write path.
.Pp
The server selects partition 1 by default.  The partition is read with the
24-byte
.Dq block:
protocol; the
.Sy LIST
reply supplies its first sector and length, so the UFS mount sees only the
partition and never the GPT headers.
A missing or corrupt UFS image is a startup error and the server exits
non-zero; it never serves a partially mounted tree.
.Sh MOUNT PROTOCOL
.Nm
opens
.Pa block:0 ,
reads
.Sy INFO
and
.Sy LIST
from it, and mounts the selected partition read-only.
It then registers the
.Dq ufs:
scheme.
A client such as
.Xr vfsd 8
mounts it with the
.Dq file:
control operation
.Sy MOUNT :
.Dl mount /ufs ufs:
After that, opening
.Pa /ufs/path
routes
.Pa path
to
.Nm .
.Pp
The server root is the filesystem root; an empty path and
.Pa /
both name it.
Paths received from
.Xr vfsd 8
have no leading slash and are treated as mount-relative.
.Pp
Symbolic links are followed with a bound of 8 links per path.
A final symbolic link is not followed for
.Sy READLINK ,
so the target is returned instead of being resolved.
.Pp
Directory reads are sequential.  The server keeps the directory cursor in the
open-file description; a client that sends a nonzero wire offset gets
.Er EINVAL .
A buffer smaller than the next packed entry also returns
.Er EINVAL .
The open-file budget is 256 descriptions.
No write, create, truncate, rename, chmod or metadata operation is accepted;
those return
.Er EROFS .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width FSD_UFS_PARTITION -compact
.It Ev FSD_UFS_DEVICE
Device path opened as a client, default
.Pa block:0 .
.It Ev FSD_UFS_PARTITION
One-based GPT partition index, default 1.  Zero mounts the whole device.
.It Ev FSD_UFS_SCHEME
Registered scheme name, default
.Dq ufs .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/fsd-ufs.toml
Service manifest.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
A missing path returns
.Er ENOENT ;
a component that is not a directory returns
.Er ENOTDIR ;
a path longer than 255 bytes or a symlink loop returns
.Er ENAMETOOLONG
or
.Er ELOOP .
A corrupt filesystem or block I/O failure returns
.Er EIO .
A write operation returns
.Er EROFS .
A protocol framing error returns
.Er EPROTO .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr blockd 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr initfsd 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr vfsd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
